From 0a077fa25fdabe22bcab90dde27e80933a0b1cdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Damman <xdamman@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:15:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(belfry): a bunker connection bound to its client key at
 creation

POST /api/user/bunker/create takes an optional client_pubkey (hex): the
connection is stored already bound to that NIP-46 client, as a
connection approved through nostr-login is. No other key can connect
with the secret from the bunker URL, so the URL is not a bearer
credential; the named client connects as usual (connect with the
secret answers ack) or just starts sending requests.

One client key, one identity: when the key is declared for or bound to
an authorization of another user in the tenant (revoked and expired
ones count), the call answers 409 with code client_key_taken and
creates nothing. The same user may get further connections for the
same client key. The check and the insert run under an advisory lock
on the client key. The response echoes client_pubkey when the binding
was made, so a caller can tell this from an older build that ignores
the field. No schema change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VBwxbHakpn87bGAgr3M5Ak
